{"content":[{"c":["SANBALLAT"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Leading political official of Samaria residing at Beth-horon in Ephraim. In a letter from Elephantine of Egypt, Sanballat was named as the governor of Samaria in 407 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},". Sanballat, along with Tobiah the Ammonite and Geshem the Arab, were adversaries of Nehemiah. They tried to prevent him from rebuilding the walls of Jerusalem during the postexilic period (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.2.10,19","r":"Neh.2.10,19","rawR":"Neh.2.10,19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.2.10,19","value":"Neh.2.10,19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 2:10, 19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.4.1,7","r":"Neh.4.1,7","rawR":"Neh.4.1,7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.4.1,7","value":"Neh.4.1,7"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:1, 7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.6.1-14","r":"Neh.6.1-14","rawR":"Neh.6.1-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.6.1-14","value":"Neh.6.1-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"6:1-14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.13.28","r":"Neh.13.28","rawR":"Neh.13.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.13.28","value":"Neh.13.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:28"},"). The Judean province probably had been included under Samaritan rule since its defeat by Babylon under Nebuchadnezzar in 586 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},". Nehemiah’s determination to rebuild the walls of Jerusalem was in essence an assertion of Judean independence from Sanballat and Samaritan control."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Sanballat","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Neh 2:10, 19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.2.10,19","rawQueryValue":"Neh.2.10,19","sourceRefExact":"Neh.2.10,19"},{"anchorText":"4:1, 7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.4.1,7","rawQueryValue":"Neh.4.1,7","sourceRefExact":"Neh.4.1,7"},{"anchorText":"6:1-14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.6.1-14","rawQueryValue":"Neh.6.1-14","sourceRefExact":"Neh.6.1-14"},{"anchorText":"13:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.13.28","rawQueryValue":"Neh.13.28","sourceRefExact":"Neh.13.28"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ee515aded5cf7cdbbb5040b5a28019d7b0e87cd3d27289c81a55a57bf68a9693","sourceItemName":"Sanballat","sourceItemOrder":53,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Sanballat","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Sanballat","title":"Sanballat","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}